I'm stopping the investigation here. The data points to one fault, and every other service is flat.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "http_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT count(*) AS n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6, 0.5) AS p50_ms, approx_quantile(duration/1e6, 0.95) AS p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'search' AND attr_span_kind = 'Client' AND span_name = 'rate.Rate/GetRates'",
          "claim": "Search's outgoing GetRates calls to rate take a median of about 1979 ms, p95 about 2722 ms, versus about 1.4 ms and 7.8 ms in normal."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT count(*) AS n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6, 0.5) AS p50_ms, approx_quantile(duration/1e6, 0.95) AS p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'rate' AND attr_span_kind = 'Server' AND span_name = 'rate.Rate/GetRates'",
          "claim": "Rate's own server spans stay sub-millisecond (p95 about 1.0 ms), matching normal, so the wait happens before rate handles the request."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT count(*) AS n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6, 0.95) AS p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'search' AND attr_span_kind = 'Client' AND span_name = 'geo.Geo/Nearby'",
          "claim": "Search's calls to geo on the same pod stay fast (p95 about 0.54 ms), so only the GetRates path is affected."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) AS n, approx_quantile(duration/1e6, 0.95) AS p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE (service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name = 'HTTP /hotels') OR (service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name = 'search.Search/Nearby' AND attr_span_kind = 'Client') GROUP BY 1, 2",
          "claim": "Frontend's /hotels server spans and its search.Search/Nearby client calls both show p95 near 2.7 s, up from about 9–18 ms in normal."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

